From: =?UTF-8?q?Emil=20W=C3=B3jcik?= <emil.wojcik@adar.pl>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:52:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] posture: send posture on launch/resume and resume the
 stream on change

posture: send posture on launch/resume and resume the stream on change

Wire the posture feature into the stream lifecycle.

NvHTTP::startApp() takes a postureQuery and appends clientPosture and
clientTouch next to clientVrrRequested on /launch and /resume; stock hosts
ignore unknown arguments. New NvHTTP::updatePosture() sends GET /posture over
the paired HTTPS path and returns the host's display_change answer when present.
tests/power/poweractions.pro now links postureclassifier.cpp because nvhttp.cpp
parses that reply.

PostureMonitor (posturemonitor.{h,cpp}) runs on a worker thread with its own
event loop: it samples the local signals once a second (the Qt event loop is not
pumped during a stream), subscribes to the KWin tabletModeChanged signal,
debounces for 1 s and reports changes with /posture. It runs in Auto mode only
and not against GFE.

The host rebuilds its virtual display only on resume, so Session ends the SDL
loop when the monitor asks for a restart, skips the host app quit and emits
restartStarting(); Session::createRestartSession() builds the resume session and
StreamSegue.qml swaps to it, which works for GUI and CLI launches alike. A
restart only happens when the host says its display must change, at most once per
60 s, never during the first 5 s, and never when the stream is already ending.
setQuitHostAppOnExit() is not part of this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
